---
import ContentPage from '../components/ContentPage.astro';
import {
  APP_NAME,
  APPLE_EULA_URL,
  APPLE_SUBSCRIPTIONS_HELP_URL,
  LEGAL_EFFECTIVE_DATE,
  PUBLISHER,
  SUPPORT_EMAIL,
} from '../data/site';
import { sitePath } from '../utils/paths';
---
<ContentPage
  pageTitle={`Terms of Use · ${APP_NAME}`}
  description={`The terms of use of ${APP_NAME}, including the Premium subscription terms.`}
  eyebrow="Legal"
  heading="Terms of Use"
>
  <p><strong>Effective date: {LEGAL_EFFECTIVE_DATE}</strong></p>
  <p>
    These terms govern your use of the {APP_NAME} iOS app ("Tracer", "the app"), published by {PUBLISHER}
    ("we", "us"). By downloading or using the app you agree to these terms and to Apple's
    <a href={APPLE_EULA_URL}>Licensed Application End User License Agreement</a> (the "Apple standard EULA"),
    which applies to the app together with these terms. If the two conflict, the Apple standard EULA wins.
  </p>

  <h2>The app</h2>
  <p>
    Tracer lets you draw the flight of a golf ball or disc onto videos on your iPhone. You can use parts of the app for
    free; other features need a Premium subscription. The app shows which features are Premium.
  </p>

  <h2>Premium subscription</h2>
  <p>Premium is an auto-renewable subscription, sold through the App Store, with these plans:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Yearly</strong>: renews every year.</li>
    <li><strong>6 months</strong>: renews every 6 months.</li>
    <li><strong>Weekly</strong>: renews every week.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The price and length of each plan, and of any free trial, are shown in the app before you confirm the purchase,
    and may differ by country.
  </p>
  <h3>Free trial</h3>
  <p>
    Some plans start with a free trial. When the trial ends, the subscription renews automatically at the plan's price
    unless you cancel at least 24 hours before the trial ends. If you buy a subscription during a free trial, any unused
    part of the trial is forfeited.
  </p>
  <h3>Payment and renewal</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Payment is charged to your Apple ID account when you confirm the purchase.</li>
    <li>
      The subscription renews automatically for the same length and price unless you cancel it at least 24 hours before
      the end of the current period.
    </li>
    <li>Your Apple ID account is charged for renewal within 24 hours before the end of the current period.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Managing and cancelling</h3>
  <p>
    You manage and cancel your subscription in your Apple ID account settings: on your iPhone, open Settings, tap your
    name, then Subscriptions (<a href={APPLE_SUBSCRIPTIONS_HELP_URL}>Apple's instructions</a>). Cancelling stops the next
    renewal; Premium stays active until the end of the period you paid for. Deleting the app or your account in the app
    does not cancel a subscription.
  </p>
  <h3>Refunds and restoring</h3>
  <p>
    Purchases are processed by Apple, and refunds are handled by Apple under its policies. If you reinstall the app or
    move to a new iPhone with the same Apple ID, tap "Restore purchases" in the app's Settings to get Premium back.
  </p>

  <h2>Your videos</h2>
  <p>
    Your videos stay yours. You are responsible for the videos you trace and share, and for having the right to use the
    people, places and sound in them. When you save a golf trace, a short clip is uploaded to improve our ball tracking,
    as described in our <a href={sitePath('/privacy')}>Privacy Policy</a>; you give us permission to store and use those
    clips for that purpose.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    Do not use the app to break the law or anyone's rights, and do not reverse engineer, resell or interfere with the app
    or our services, except as the law allows.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>Our <a href={sitePath('/privacy')}>Privacy Policy</a> explains what the app collects and how we use it.</p>

  <h2>Disclaimers and liability</h2>
  <p>
    The app is provided "as is". Automatic ball tracking may miss or misplace a ball or disc, and you can always adjust a
    trace by hand. To the extent the law allows, our liability is limited as set out in the Apple standard EULA.
    Nothing in these terms limits rights you have under consumer law that cannot be waived.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. We post changes on this page and update the effective date; if a change is material,
    we tell you in the app before it takes effect.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>{PUBLISHER} · <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a></p>
</ContentPage>
